  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35733844",
      "title": "Exploring an Alternative Way of Defining Routes",
      "sourceHash": "243fe4903703630c04e81ad330f8f53f7d71efdbfa1d1858a7d558ffee336e66",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 5.286,
          "en": "So we now added our first two route definitions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.286,
          "end": 7.086,
          "en": "There is of course way more we can and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.086,
          "end": 10.402,
          "en": "we should do when building a page that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.402,
          "end": 13.38,
          "en": "or a website that supports routing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.38,
          "end": 16.44,
          "en": "But before we do that, I wanna show you an alternative way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.44,
          "end": 18.933,
          "en": "of defining your routes here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.77,
          "end": 22.26,
          "en": "You can define them like this with an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.26,
          "end": 24,
          "en": "of route definition objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24,
          "end": 27.93,
          "en": "And in my opinion, this is quite an intuitive approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.93,
          "end": 30.78,
          "en": "But especially if you worked with older versions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.78,
          "end": 32.687,
          "en": "of react-router-dom, it might also be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.687,
          "end": 35.43,
          "en": "a bit of a strange approach because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.43,
          "end": 38.042,
          "en": "in older versions you actually defined all your",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.042,
          "end": 42.84,
          "en": "routes with help of components and JSX code instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.84,
          "end": 45.84,
          "en": "of JavaScript Objects in array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.84,
          "end": 49.17,
          "en": "And you can still do this in this version here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.17,
          "end": 51.12,
          "en": "in this latest version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.12,
          "end": 53.22,
          "en": "You can import another function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.22,
          "end": 55.41,
          "en": "from react-router-dom, and that's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.41,
          "end": 58.383,
          "en": "the create routes from elements function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.4,
          "end": 64.02,
          "en": "And you can create a new constant call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.02,
          "end": 65.699,
          "en": "route definitions, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.699,
          "end": 68.726,
          "en": "and call create routes from elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.726,
          "end": 73.726,
          "en": "and to dysfunction, you pass a bunch of JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.22,
          "end": 77.06700000000001,
          "en": "To be precise, you import a route component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.06700000000001,
          "end": 82.06700000000001,
          "en": "from react-router-dom, and then here you can add your",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.467,
          "end": 87.467,
          "en": "route component like this to create routs from elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.81,
          "end": 91.71000000000001,
          "en": "With one wrapper route, you could then add your nested",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.71000000000001,
          "end": 95.91,
          "en": "routes here where every route receives a path prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.91,
          "end": 98.45,
          "en": "like slash nothing, and an element prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.45,
          "end": 102.663,
          "en": "which could, for example, load the homepage JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.86,
          "end": 106.8,
          "en": "So of course you might see that this line is the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.8,
          "end": 108.78,
          "en": "as this route definition down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.78,
          "end": 112.22999999999999,
          "en": "Just with JSX code and components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.22999999999999,
          "end": 114.21000000000001,
          "en": "And we can do the same here for products,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.21000000000001,
          "end": 117.84,
          "en": "and the product page, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.84,
          "end": 119.85,
          "en": "And with that, you are defining all your",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.85,
          "end": 123.903,
          "en": "routes with help of JSX code instead of objects in an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.28,
          "end": 127.784,
          "en": "You can then take those route definitions created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.784,
          "end": 130.86,
          "en": "with create routes from elements and use that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.86,
          "end": 133.41,
          "en": "to create your browser router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.41,
          "end": 135.57,
          "en": "So if I quickly comment this out,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.57,
          "end": 138.652,
          "en": "we could also create our router now by calling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.652,
          "end": 141.87,
          "en": "create browser router, but instead of passing this array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.87,
          "end": 144.09,
          "en": "of route definition objects to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.09,
          "end": 146.014,
          "en": "we pass the route definitions that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.014,
          "end": 148.75,
          "en": "were created with create routes from elements to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.75,
          "end": 149.913,
          "en": "this router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.78,
          "end": 152.88,
          "en": "With that, if we save that, we still get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.88,
          "end": 156.071,
          "en": "our homepage and we can still visit slash products,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.071,
          "end": 158.485,
          "en": "but now we're using this different approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.485,
          "end": 161.31,
          "en": "of defining our routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.31,
          "end": 163.89,
          "en": "Ultimately, it is up to you what you prefer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.89,
          "end": 167.61,
          "en": "I'll switch back to this object-based solution,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.61,
          "end": 171.42000000000002,
          "en": "but you could also define your routes with JSX code instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 171.42000000000002,
          "end": 172.773,
          "en": "if you preferred that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.7,
          "end": 176.22,
          "en": "I'll comment out all the parts related to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.22,
          "end": 177.27,
          "en": "because as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 177.27,
          "end": 179.553,
          "en": "I'll stick to this object based approach.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
